# Every supply with nowhere to put its excess and demand nobody could serve, beside who is named as
# having gone without. One row per examined layer, `violates` where no unserved holder appears, or,
# under interference, where any holder claims the excess was served.
#
# The argument is in the word "every"
#   If every buffer was accounted for and none of them had room, the excess above the nameplate
#   cannot have been absorbed by running hot, by drawing on stock or by making the demand wait.
#   There was nowhere to go, so it went unserved and somebody has to be named as having gone
#   without. One unmeasured buffer licenses none of this, whatever the other two say, because
#   nobody knows what that route could have taken. layers/exposure_scope.sqlc classifies all
#   three standings; this rule reads the one that concludes anything.
#
# Under interference, every holder; under transition, one
#   Where the whole demand range sits above the nameplate, all of the remainder is excess, so every
#   holder is `customer` or `unrealised`: a `booked`, `counterparty` or `people` holder says part of
#   an excess was absorbed by a supply that had nowhere to absorb it. Where the ranges overlap,
#   part of the range is genuinely clearance and a `booked` share is legitimate there, so the rule
#   weakens to presence: at least one holder bears the unserved part. The fit is the one derived
#   from the ranges, which checks/fit_disagrees holds the filed sign to.
#
# Every buffer, not the capacity alone
#   A measured-zero capacity slack does not make an excess unabsorbable while stock or waiting
#   could still take it. Read on the capacity buffer alone, this rule would accuse a filing whose
#   inventory slack took part of the excess and says so with a `booked` holder.
#
# One relation, three readings
#   The violation is an anti-join against entries/unserved_holders.sqlc, which the clearance
#   check semi-joins and the exposure check sums, and a semi-join against
#   entries/served_holders.sqlc under interference.
-- every slack on the layer accounted for and empty, against pm:HolderKind of every holder.
SELECT r.rule, p.filing, p.layer, p.violates, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(checks/roster.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT c.filing, c.layer,
           u.filing IS NULL OR (c.derived_fit = 'interference' AND s.filing IS NOT NULL) AS violates,
           CASE WHEN u.filing IS NULL
                THEN format('%s could not be served and no holder says so', c.exposure)
                WHEN c.derived_fit = 'interference' AND s.filing IS NOT NULL
                THEN format('%s could not be served, and a %s holder says part of it was',
                            c.exposure, s.kinds)
                ELSE format('%s could not be served, and the holders say who went without',
                            c.exposure)
           END AS detail
    FROM (
        SELECT e.filing, e.layer, e.exposure, e.derived_fit
        FROM (
            :compose(layers/unabsorbed_exposure.sqlc)
        ) e
        WHERE e.exposure > 1e-9
    ) c
    LEFT JOIN ( SELECT DISTINCT filing, layer
                FROM (
                    :compose(entries/unserved_holders.sqlc)
                ) h ) u USING (filing, layer)
    LEFT JOIN (
        :compose(folds/served_totals.sqlc)
    ) s USING (filing, layer)
) p ON true
WHERE r.slug = 'nobody_named_as_unserved'
